{The knight to the edge, on its way to c5. It keeps the centre closed on Black's terms: after d5 the knight hits e4 from c5 and there is no knight on c6 to be chased. The famous 7...Nc6 8.d5 Ne7 is a race both sides have to know to move twenty, and this course declines it in favour of the plan that fits every other chapter. [%tags development vs-classical]}
( 7... Nc6!?
{Sound and the heaviest theory in the opening: 8.d5 Ne7 and a race of pawn storms where one wrong move loses. The fork rule takes the knight to a6, where the plans are the ones the rest of the course uses.}
